sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: rule 1 (read-only from Node agent reports, like tool.adopt), R1 record-only branch, R4 Node-work branch like tool.remove; .env stays the user's file; Processes from Project definitions for development (instance.create). docs/domains/applications.md#register-an-existing-checkout.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 5, 16, 22 (no Node re-read of admitted facts; cfgmgmt file mode, ssh exec setup, cfgmgmt systemd Processes).
  %% status: draft
  %% Interim: until the Node agent reports checkouts, every registration starts a run that reads the checkout over @swamp/ssh, and the Gateway checks the read facts at the end. --setup stays refused (operation.kind_unavailable).
  %% command: instance:register
  %% kind: instance.register
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane A icon=server pill=observer tone=amber
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>on Node 12
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant A as Node agent<br/>orbit-agent
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  loop continuously, on change (later)
    Note over A: Observe checkouts<br/>under the apps root
    %%> Later:
    %%> - this observation lands in the Node agent's observer pass; today the agent watches only task checkouts, at most 64 per Node
    %%> - until then, `instance:register` keeps its Swamp read of the checkout over `@swamp/ssh`
    %%> What it observes:
    %%> - each Git checkout under `<apps-root>/<project-slug>/<name>`
    %%> - its owner, Git layout, origin, branch and `HEAD` commit, and whether it is dirty
    %%> - whether `.env` exists and who can read it
    %%> - application facts: PHP version and whether it is Laravel
    %%> Runs as:
    %%> - read-only; the Node agent never changes a Node
    A->>GW: Report observations<br/>with observed_at
    %%> What it sends:
    %%> - what changed since the last report, with the time it was observed
    Note over GW: Store latest facts<br/>per Node, per checkout
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway always has a recent picture of the checkouts on each app-dev Node
  end
  CLI->>GW: instance:register<br/>--project=7 --name=feature --yes
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `cd /fast/apps/acme/feature && orbit instance:register --project=7 --name=feature --yes`
  %%> - syntax: `--project=ID [--path=PATH] [--name=NAME] [--root=PATH] [--setup] [--yes] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> What registering means:
  %%> - Orbit adopts a checkout that already exists, in place
  %%> - Orbit owns the source from now on; a later `instance:destroy` deletes the checkout
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--yes`, the CLI asks for consent that names the source; the default is No
  %%> - without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--yes` is required
  %%> CLI checks first:
  %%> - the directory is a Git checkout, and its origin has no credentials
  Note over GW: Check against the facts<br/>path · origin · branch · commit
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the request comes from Node 12 itself; the Node that sends it receives the Instance
  %%> - Node 12 has the `app-dev` role, and Project 7 may be placed on it
  %%> - the name `feature` is free in Project 7
  %%> Checks in the agent's latest report:
  %%> - the checkout is at `/fast/apps/acme/feature` and the Node's managed user owns it
  %%> - its origin is Project 7's repository
  %%> - it is a plain checkout, not a linked worktree
  %%> - the report is fresh enough to trust
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether the Node needs work, or only a record
  alt no --setup, .env private
    Note over GW: Record the Instance<br/>R1: no task, no run
    %%> When:
    %%> - no `--setup`, and `.env` is absent or readable only by its owner
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 recorded as active, with the observed branch, commit and application facts
    %%> - Git `HEAD`, the index, dirty files and `.env` stay as they are
    %%> - no Swamp run starts (R1)
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - no Process starts; use `--setup`, or `instance:setup` later
    GW-->>CLI: Instance registered<br/>Instance 42 · branch feature
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else --setup or public .env
    Note over GW: Reserve, record intent<br/>Instance 42 · task #5131
    %%> When:
    %%> - `--setup` was given, or the agent saw a `.env` that others can read
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Instance 42 recorded as reserved, with the observed facts
    %%> - task #5131 recorded with the full intent
    %%> Today:
    %%> - `--setup` returns `operation.kind_unavailable`
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-register
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    %%> - the observed facts, the setup steps, the development Process definitions
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5131
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    SW->>N: Read the checkout files<br/>sh -c · digest, profile
    %%> Interim:
    %%> - these eight reads replace the agent's report until its observer pass lands; each is one `@swamp/ssh` exec argv
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - one read of the file tree digest, the `artisan` entry point and `composer.json`
    SW->>N: Read the Git top level<br/>git rev-parse · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - the checkout's top-level directory
    SW->>N: Read the Git common dir<br/>git rev-parse · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - the shared `.git` directory; a linked worktree has another one
    SW->>N: List the worktrees<br/>git worktree list · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - every worktree of the repository
    SW->>N: Read the origin<br/>git config · masked · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - the origin URL, with any embedded credential masked before it leaves the Node
    SW->>N: Read the branch<br/>git branch · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - the checked-out branch, empty when `HEAD` is detached
    SW->>N: Read the commit<br/>git rev-parse HEAD · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - the `HEAD` commit
    SW->>N: Read the default branch<br/>git for-each-ref · interim
    %%> What it reads:
    %%> - the remote default branch
    SW->>N: Protect the .env file<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · go-rwx
    %%> How:
    %%> - one `chmod go-rwx` argv on a regular `.env`, safe to repeat
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - removes group and public access from `.env`
    %%> Interim:
    %%> - runs after the reads, before the Gateway checks them; a refused source keeps the tighter mode
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - never reads or changes the content; the file stays the user's
    %%> Later, with --setup:
    %%> - Run Project setup steps (`@swamp/ssh` exec, in order), then Create, start Processes (`@swamp/cfgmgmt/systemd`, forEach)
    alt all steps pass
      N-->>SW: steps passed
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - every step passed
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Check facts, record<br/>Instance 42 → active
      %%> What it checks (interim):
      %%> - the top level is the checkout, its `.git` is its own, and it is the only worktree
      %%> - the origin is Project 7's repository; a masked origin is refused (`instance.source_identity_invalid`)
      %%> - `composer.json` and the entry point give a supported PHP version and the Laravel flag
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Instance 42 becomes active with the read branch, commit and application facts; task #5131 succeeds
      %%> - a mismatch fails task #5131 and keeps Instance 42 reserved (`instance.registration_conflict`)
    else a step fails
      N--xSW: mismatch or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - the checkout no longer matches, or a setup or Process step fails
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code
      Note over GW: Keep Instance, mark failed<br/>rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Instance 42 stays, marked failed; task #5131 fails
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the checkout stays as it is; no rollback
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the same command again; it is a new task
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5131
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  else facts mismatch or too old
    GW--xCLI: Refused or can't verify<br/>instance.source_invalid
    %%> When:
    %%> - the path, owner, origin or layout doesn't match, or the agent hasn't reported recently
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is recorded; fix the source, or try again when the agent reports
  end
